Gradle is running with a warm cache. Good. Let me start writing code now.

First: LlmClient.kt rewrite.

Key design points:
- `chat(messages, tools, isCancelled, onDelta)`.
- streaming with fallback.
- retries.

Let me write it.

```kotlin
package dev.pocketrun.agent

import org.json.JSONArray
import org.json.JSONObject
import java.io.BufferedReader
import java.io.IOException
import java.net.HttpURLConnection
import java.net.SocketTimeoutException
import java.net.URL

class LlmClient(private val config: AgentSettings.Config) {

    data class ToolCall(val id: String, val name: String, val arguments: String)
    data class Response(val content: String?, val toolCalls: List<ToolCall>)

    class LlmException(message: String) : Exception(message)

    /** Thrown when the streamed answer turns out to be unusable; the caller retries without streaming. */
    private class EmptyAnswerException : Exception("пустой ответ модели")

    companion object {
        const val CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000
        /** 15 minutes: long generations and slow gateways must not kill a turn. */
        const val READ_TIMEOUT_MS = 900_000
        const val MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3
        const val RETRY_BACKOFF_MS = 3_000L

        fun models(baseUrl, apiKey): List<String> { ... }

        // --- SSE parsing, extracted for tests
        internal class StreamAccumulator { ... }
    }
}
```

For testability, I'll make the SSE accumulation a separate internal class in the same file or a new file `LlmStream.kt`. Let me put it in LlmClient.kt as a nested internal class so tests can reach it (`LlmClient.StreamAccumulator`) — tests are in the same package `dev.pocketrun.agent`, so internal access works within the module... Actually, Kotlin `internal` is module-scoped; the unit test source set is a "friend" of the main source set in Gradle Kotlin plugin (associated compilation), so `internal` is accessible from unit tests. Yes, the Android/Kotlin plugin sets up test as a friend module. The existing tests access `MiniShell.tokenize` which is `internal` — confirming this works.

Now write the code.

```kotlin
    /**
     * One chat completion. Streams by default (SSE) so long generations keep
     * the connection alive and the user sees progress; falls back to a plain
     * request when the server ignores `stream`. Transient failures (timeout,
     * 429, 5xx) are retried with a backoff.
     */
    fun chat(
        messages: JSONArray,
        tools: JSONArray?,
        isCancelled: () -> Boolean = { false },
        onDelta: ((String) -> Unit)? = null,
    ): Response {
        var last: Throwable? = null
        for (attempt in 1..MAX_ATTEMPTS) {
            if (isCancelled()) throw LlmException(CANCELLED)
            try {
                return request(messages, tools, stream = true, isCancelled, onDelta)
            } catch (e: EmptyAnswerException) {
                // The server answered, but not in a way we can use: ask again
                // without streaming (some proxies answer 200 with an HTML error).
                try {
                    return request(messages, tools, stream = false, isCancelled, null)
                } catch (t: Throwable) { ... }
            } catch (e: Throwable) {
                ...
            }
        }
    }
```

Let me structure it more cleanly:

```kotlin
    fun chat(messages, tools, isCancelled = {false}, onDelta = null): Response {
        var attempt = 0
        var stream = true
        var delayMs = RETRY_BACKOFF_MS
        while (true) {
            attempt++
            if (isCancelled()) throw LlmException(CANCELLED)
            try {
                return request(messages, tools, stream, isCancelled, onDelta)
            } catch (e: Throwable) {
                val reason = describe(e)
                // A server that answered with something unusable: retry once,
                // this time as a plain (non-streamed) request.
                if (e is StreamUnsupported) {
                    if (!stream) throw LlmException(reason)
                    stream = false
                    attempt--   // the fallback is part of the same attempt
                    continue
                }
                if (attempt >= MAX_ATTEMPTS || !isRetryable(e)) throw LlmException(reason)
                sleep(delayMs, isCancelled)   // interruptible
                delayMs *= 2
            }
        }
    }
```

Where `StreamUnsupported` is thrown when the response is neither SSE with content nor a parseable JSON body.

Retryable: SocketTimeoutException, IOException (connect resets), HttpException with 408/429/5xx. I'll define a private class HttpStatusException(status, body) for HTTP error responses so retry logic can inspect the status, and `describe()` produces the Russian message.

Note the previous behavior: HTTP errors threw LlmException with "HTTP $status от url: body". Keep the message format so the VM's `"403" in event.message` check still works.

Now `request`:

```kotlin
    private fun request(messages, tools, stream: Boolean, isCancelled, onDelta): Response {
        val body = JSONObject().apply {
            put("model", config.model)
            put("messages", messages)
            put("temperature", 0.2)
            if (tools != null && tools.length() > 0) {
                put("tools", tools)
                put("tool_choice", "auto")
            }
            if (stream) put("stream", true)
        }
        val conn = open(body, stream)
        try {
            val status = conn.responseCode
            if (status !in 200..299) {
                val err = readAll(conn.errorStream)
                throw HttpStatusException(status, err)
            }
            return readAnswer(conn, isCancelled, onDelta)
        } finally {
            conn.disconnect()
        }
    }
```

`readAnswer(conn, ...)`: line-based dispatch.

```kotlin
    private fun readAnswer(conn: HttpURLConnection, isCancelled: () -> Boolean, onDelta: ((String)->Unit)?): Response {
        val reader = conn.inputStream.bufferedReader(Charsets.UTF_8)
        val acc = StreamAccumulator(onDelta)
        var sawSse = false
        val plain = StringBuilder()
        while (true) {
            if (isCancelled()) throw LlmException(CANCELLED)
            val line = reader.readLine() ?: break
            if (line.isEmpty()) continue
            if (line.startsWith(SSE_DATA)) {
                sawSse = true
                val payload = line.removePrefix(SSE_DATA).trim()
                if (payload == SSE_DONE) break
                acc.feed(payload)
            } else if (!sawSse) {
                // Not a stream: the whole body is a plain JSON response.
                plain.append(line).append('\n')
            }
        }
        if (!sawSse) return parseCompletion(JSONObject(plain.toString().trim()))  // may throw StreamUnsupported
        return acc.result()
    }
```

Careful: if a non-SSE body arrives, we accumulate lines; at the end parse as JSON. If parsing fails (e.g. HTML error page with 200), throw StreamUnsupported. Then chat() retries without streaming... but that would return the same HTML. Hmm, if the JSON parse fails, the fallback also fails → then it throws LlmException with the body snippet. Acceptable, and it makes the error message informative (include the first 200 chars of the body).

Also: if the SSE stream yields no content and no tool calls (e.g. an `error` event or an immediate `data: [DONE]`) → `acc.result()` returns empty → treat as StreamUnsupported? If the stream contained only a `data: [DONE]`, that's an empty answer from the model. Retrying non-streaming might give the real answer (or an error message). Let me throw StreamUnsupported when the accumulator is empty, so we get one non-streaming attempt. But careful: the non-streaming attempt would return a valid non-empty response typically. If both are empty → after the fallback, `result()` empty → throw LlmException("модель вернула пустой ответ"). And in the agent, an empty answer triggers a nudge+continue. Fine.

Also handle the SSE `error` payload: `data: {"error":{"message":"..."}}` → throw LlmException with that message. And OpenAI-style error inside 200 responses: `{"error": {...}}` in a plain body.

`StreamAccumulator.feed(payload)`:
```kotlin
        fun feed(payload: String) {
            val json = try { JSONObject(payload) } catch (t: Throwable) { return }
            json.optJSONObject("error")?.let { err ->
                throw LlmException("ошибка модели: " + (err.optString("message").ifEmpty { payload.take(200) }))
            }
            val choices = json.optJSONArray("choices") ?: return
            val choice = choices.optJSONObject(0) ?: return
            val delta = choice.optJSONObject("delta") ?: choice.optJSONObject("message")
            if (delta == null) return
            delta.optString("content").takeIf { it.isNotEmpty() }?.let {
                text.append(it)
                onDelta?.invoke(it)
            }
            // reasoning models stream their thinking in a separate field
            delta.optString("reasoning_content").takeIf { it.isNotEmpty() }?.let { reasoning.append(it) }
            val calls = delta.optJSONArray("tool_calls") ?: return
            for (i in 0 until calls.length()) {
                val c = calls.optJSONObject(i) ?: continue
                val idx = c.optInt("index", i)
                val slot = toolCalls.getOrPut(idx) { ToolCallBuilder() }
                c.optString("id").takeIf { it.isNotEmpty() }?.let { slot.id = it }
                val fn = c.optJSONObject("function")
                if (fn != null) {
                    fn.optString("name").takeIf { it.isNotEmpty() }?.let { slot.name += it } // hmm, += or =?
                    slot.arguments.append(fn.optString("arguments"))
                }
            }
        }
```
Note: for the name, streaming sends the name once (in the first chunk) — use `if (slot.name.isEmpty()) slot.name = it else slot.name += it` to be safe with servers that split. Names are short; concatenation is safe.

result():
```kotlin
        fun result(): Response {
            val calls = toolCalls.entries.sortedBy { it.key }.map { (i, b) ->
                ToolCall(id = b.id.ifEmpty { "call_$i" }, name = b.name, arguments = b.arguments.toString().ifBlank { "{}" })
            }.filter { it.name.isNotEmpty() }
            if (calls.isEmpty() && text.isBlank()) throw StreamUnsupported()  // hmm
            val content = text.toString().ifBlank { null }
            return Response(content, calls)
